---
layout: layouts/page
title: AI/AN Medicaid exemption scorecard
permalink: /aian-medicaid-scorecard/
description: How closely each state's published Medicaid policy follows CMS rules for American Indians and Alaska Natives under the new work and renewal requirements.
---
{% set sc = aianScorecard %}
{% from "aian-dots.njk" import dots %}
{% if not sc.rubric.approved %}
<div class="usa-alert usa-alert--warning usa-alert--slim"><div class="usa-alert__body"><p class="usa-alert__text"><strong>Draft.</strong> Grades are provisional while the rubric is under review and evidence is re-verified.</p></div></div>
{% endif %}

<h1>American Indian and Alaska Native Medicaid exemption scorecard</h1>
{% set sm = sc.summary %}
<p class="usa-intro aian-headline">Only <strong>{{ sm.allMet }} of {{ sm.subject }}</strong> states meet all {{ sm.total }} requirements in their published policy. The median state meets <strong>{{ sm.median }}</strong>, and <strong>{{ sm.anyContradiction }}</strong> publish policy that contradicts at least one.</p>

<p>Federal law exempts American Indians and Alaska Natives from Medicaid's new work requirement and keeps their renewals at 12 months. This scorecard grades how closely each state's <strong>published</strong> policy follows the CMS rules that carry out those protections. It measures what states have written down, not what happens at every eligibility office.</p>

<p>Grades update as states publish new policy. A state, tribe, or Indian health program can <a href="{{ '/aian-medicaid-scorecard/process/' | url }}">submit evidence</a> on any state's page. Last checked {{ sc.lastChecked }}.</p>

<h2>By the numbers</h2>
<ul class="usa-list">
  <li><strong>{{ sm.allMet }} of {{ sm.subject }}</strong> states subject to the new rules meet all {{ sm.total }} requirements in their published policy.</li>
  <li>The median state meets <strong>{{ sm.median }} of {{ sm.total }}</strong>.</li>
  <li><strong>{{ sm.anyContradiction }}</strong> states publish policy that contradicts at least one requirement.</li>
  <li><strong>{{ sm.tribalChannel }}</strong> states publish a way for tribes or Indian health programs to confirm a person's status.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="how-grades-change">How a state raises its grade</h2>
<ol class="usa-list">
  <li><strong>Publish a qualifying policy.</strong> Each state's page lists every requirement it does not yet meet, the policy that would meet it, model language from a state that already does, and the grade the state would reach.</li>
  <li><strong>Send us the public link.</strong> Use the Submit evidence button on the state's page. A state agency, tribe, Indian health program, or anyone else can submit, and evidence from tribes and Indian health programs counts the same as the state's.</li>
  <li><strong>We review within {{ sc.rubric.submission.review_business_days }} business days.</strong> The state's page shows Evidence under review until we finish.</li>
  <li><strong>The grade updates.</strong> An upgrade publishes right away. A downgrade waits {{ sc.rubric.submission.downgrade_notice_days }} days after we notify the state. Every change is listed in the state's history with its date and source.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Grades at a glance</h2>
<ul class="usa-list">
{% for c in sc.counts %}{% if c.n > 0 %}<li><strong>{{ c.grade }}</strong>: {{ c.n }} {% if c.n == 1 %}state{% else %}states{% endif %}</li>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
</ul>

<h2>All states, ranked</h2>
<p>Ranked by requirements met, then fewest contradicted, then fewest unpublished. The grade follows mechanically from those counts (see <a href="#rubric">How grades work</a>).</p>
{% set im = sc.rubric.impact %}
<p class="aian-legend"><strong>Impact</strong> is drawn to scale: each {{ dots(1, 0) }} is {{ im.dot_size | aianNum }} American Indian and Alaska Native people we estimate could be exempt, and a partly filled dot shows the remainder, like a clock face: for example {{ dots(0, 0.25) }} is 2,500. It is the 2020 Census American Indian and Alaska Native population times an assumed {{ (im.subject_share * 100) | round }}% who are expansion adults subject to the work rule; no published source gives that share. <strong>To fix</strong> lists every requirement the state does not meet: contradictions first, then requirements with no published policy. Each links to the fix on the state's page.</p>
<table class="usa-table usa-table--borderless usa-table--stacked aian-roster">
  <caption class="usa-sr-only">States ranked by requirements met, with grade, estimated impact, and the requirements each state still needs to fix</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">Score</th><th scope="col">Grade</th><th scope="col">Impact</th><th scope="col">To fix</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for s in sc.ranked %}
    {% set url = ('/aian-medicaid-scorecard/' + s.slug + '/') | url %}
    <tr>
      <th scope="row" data-label="State"><a href="{{ url }}">{{ s.name }}</a>{% if s.under_review %} <span class="usa-tag">Evidence under review</span>{% endif %}</th>
      <td data-label="Score">{% if s.status != 'not_subject' %}<strong>{{ s.met }}/{{ sc.summary.total }}</strong><br><span class="text-base aian-sub">{{ s.contradicts }} contradicted, {{ s.unpublished }} unpublished</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td data-label="Grade">{{ s.grade }}{% if s.status == 'not_subject' and not s.confirmed %} (to confirm){% endif %}</td>
      <td data-label="Impact">{% if s.status != 'not_subject' %}<span role="img" aria-label="about {{ s.impact.estimate | aianNum }} estimated">{{ dots(s.impact.full, s.impact.part) }}</span><br><span class="text-base">about {{ s.impact.estimate | aianNum }}</span>{% if s.impact.published %}<br><span class="text-base">State reports {{ s.impact.published.count | aianNum }} <a href="{{ s.impact.published.url }}">verified</a></span>{% endif %}{% endif %}</td>
      <td data-label="To fix">{% if s.status == 'not_subject' %}Not subject{% elif not s.improvements.length %}Nothing{% else %}{% set con = s.fixContradicts %}{% set unp = s.fixUnpublished %}{% if con.length %}<span class="aian-fix-kind">Contradicts:</span> {% for i in con %}<a href="{{ url }}#fix-{{ i.id }}">{{ i.short }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% if con.length and unp.length %}<br>{% endif %}{% if unp.length %}<span class="aian-fix-kind">Not published:</span> {% for i in unp %}<a href="{{ url }}#fix-{{ i.id }}">{{ i.short }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endif %}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="rubric">How grades work</h2>
<p>Each state is checked against {{ aianScorecard.rubric.requirements.length }} requirements. For each one, published state policy either <strong>meets</strong> it, <strong>contradicts</strong> it, or has <strong>not published</strong> anything. Silence never counts as meeting a requirement.</p>
<table class="usa-table usa-table--borderless">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Requirement</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{% for r in sc.rubric.requirements %}<tr><td>{{ r.label }}</td><td>{{ r.citation }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table>
<table class="usa-table usa-table--borderless">
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Grade</th><th scope="col">Rule</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>{% for g in sc.rubric.grades %}<tr><td>{{ g.grade }}</td><td>{{ g.rule }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table>
<p>We also report, but do not grade, {% for b in sc.rubric.best_practices %}{{ b.label | lower }} ({{ b.citation | lower }}){% endfor %}.</p>
